<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jean-Baptiste du Casse</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1646–1715</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Jean-Baptiste Ducasse</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jean-Baptiste du Casse was a French naval commander, buccaneer and colonial governor. In 1689 he led an unsuccessful attack on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a>, and as governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-domingue">Saint-Domingue</a> from 1691 to 1700 he took part in the capture of Cartagena in 1697. He later commanded French squadrons in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a> and became a lieutenant-general of the navy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jean-baptiste-du-casse.jpg" alt="Jean-Baptiste du Casse" width="320" height="491" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Hyacinthe Rigaud · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jean_Baptiste_du_Casse.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
